  "id": "DrugBank_DB00443 - MONDO_5062",
  "verbalization": "Betamethasone is implicated in the development of lymphoma through a series of indirect pathways that involve steroid hormones and their effects on the immune system. The evidence suggests that Betamethasone, through its indication for Miliary Tuberculosis and Musculoskeletal System Disease, ultimately leads to Lymphoma via Methylprednisolone, which is a metabolite of Betamethasone. This connection is further supported by the indication of Methylprednisolone in Lymphoma, indicating a potential role in immune modulation or inflammatory response. The presence of multiple pathways linking Betamethasone to Lymphoma highlights a possible dependency on corticosteroids in the pathogenesis of lymphoma, suggesting that the steroid receptor pathway may be a key mechanism. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of corticosteroids in the development of lymphoma, particularly through their effects on immune cell function and inflammation.",
